Backport of the upstream sass fix for C++ exceptions under Emscripten: pull request
https://github.com/rstudio/sass/pull/155 ("Fix throwing exceptions under Emscripten",
commit a8d149b, after 0.4.10 and not yet on CRAN; MIT). src/Makevars hands libsass's
own Makefile CFLAGS but not CXXFLAGS, so libsass's C++ is compiled without
-fwasm-exceptions, and the first Sass error -- which libsass raises as a C++ exception
-- aborts webR instead of becoming an R error. rwasm's `uname` reports Emscripten, so
the hunk applies inside the build image. rwasm builds sass from that commit for
repo.r-wasm.org (its webr-remotes list), hence the .9000 there.
`patch` ignores this text before the first diff header.

--- a/src/libsass/Makefile
+++ b/src/libsass/Makefile
@@ -73,6 +73,10 @@ else
 	STATIC_LIBSTDCPP ?= 0
 endif
 
+ifeq (Emscripten,$(UNAME))
+	CXXFLAGS += -fwasm-exceptions
+endif
+
 ifndef SASS_LIBSASS_PATH
 	SASS_LIBSASS_PATH = .
 endif
